# PrintPulse release checklist
# Build and publish with the local SDK — CloudPebble is not required.

## 0. Pick the version
- [ ] Choose the new semver (e.g. 1.1.0). Call it NEW below.
- [ ] Skim git status / diff; only ship what you mean to ship.

## 1. Bump the built-in version (before building)
Keep these three equal to NEW:
- [ ] `package.json` → `"version"`
- [ ] `src/pkjs/version.js` → `APP_VERSION`
- [ ] `version.json` → `"version"`
      Optional: update `"message"` (banner text) and `"url"` (usually
      https://github.com/TechJeeper/PrintPulse/releases/latest).

## 2. One-time appstore login (per machine / SDK volume)
- [ ] `./build.ps1 -Login`
      Signs into your Pebble account inside the container; the session stays
      in the `pebble-sdk` volume. Or set `PEBBLE_FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN` for CI.

## 3. Build + publish to the Pebble appstore
- [ ] Refresh screenshots in `store/screenshots/` if the UI changed
      (names must be `emery_….png`, `basalt_….png`, `diorite_….png`, `flint_….png`).
- [ ] Edit `store/listing.json` only if the name / description / category changed
      (category key: `tools`, `daily`, `notifications`, `remotes`, `health`, or `games`).
- [ ] `./build.ps1 -Publish -ReleaseNotes "Short user-facing notes"`
      → builds `build/PrintPulse.pbw`
      → runs `pebble publish` with listing + screenshots (no emulator, no CloudPebble)
- [ ] First-ever listing: if non-interactive fails, use
      `./build.ps1 -Publish -InteractivePublish -ReleaseNotes "…"` once.
- [ ] Confirm the listing at https://apps.repebble.com (or the Developer Dashboard).

Optional extras (same command can combine flags):
- [ ] `./build.ps1 -Zip` → also writes `dist/PrintPulse-cloudpebble.zip`
- [ ] `./build.ps1 -Phone <ip>` → install on a watch after build

## 4. Smoke-check (optional but recommended)
- [ ] Install on a watch (`./build.ps1 -Phone <ip>` or open the `.pbw` in the Pebble app).
- [ ] Open Settings once; confirm printers / theme still look right.

## 5. Commit and push to GitHub
- [ ] Commit version bumps + code + regenerated `config_page.js` if needed
      (+ updated `store/screenshots` if you changed them).
- [ ] Push to `main` (installed apps read
      `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TechJeeper/PrintPulse/main/version.json`).
- [ ] Pushing `version.json` with NEW is what triggers the in-app “update available”
      toast / Settings banner for people still on an older build.

## 6. GitHub Release (source / sideload)
- [ ] Create a release/tag `vNEW` on https://github.com/TechJeeper/PrintPulse/releases
- [ ] Paste the same release notes you used for the appstore.
- [ ] Attach `build/PrintPulse.pbw` (and the CloudPebble zip only if you still want it).

## 7. After publish
- [ ] Open raw `version.json` on main and confirm `"version"` is NEW.
- [ ] On a phone still running the old build: reopen PrintPulse → toast once,
      Settings shows the banner; Dismiss stays quiet until a later NEW.

## Notes
- Appstore publish and GitHub are separate: `pebble publish` updates
  apps.repebble.com; pushing `version.json` notifies existing sideload/dev installs.
- Order: build/publish with bumped `APP_VERSION`, then push `version.json`.
  New builds must already contain NEW or they will keep prompting themselves.
- Do not bump `version.json` above what you actually published.
- Dismiss is per version in the phone’s localStorage; a newer `version.json`
  shows the notice again.
- Icons: leave absent to auto-generate, or add `store/icon-small.png` (80×80)
  and `store/icon-large.png` (144×144).
